    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "837beecf-4239-4b3d-b683-1d611af3da2e",
      "key": "e5fe3f93-c36b-4c39-8c9b-d56c4e813d6a",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "featurePropertyFeatureTitle",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Itinerary"
        },
        {
          "alias": "richTextContent",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Ch3\u003EDay 1\u003C/h3\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EWe meet at Gatwick Airport for our direct scheduled Easyjet flight to Barcelona. On arrival we are met by our tour manager and transfer by private executive coach to the centrally located 4* Catalonia Ramblas Hotel in Barcelona for a four night stay. A welcome dinner is included in our hotel this evening.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Ch3\u003EDay 2\u003C/h3\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EThis morning we enjoy an included guided coach tour of Barcelona. Our first stop is Gaudi\u2019s Parc Guell. Built between 1910 and 1914 and commissioned by Eusebi G\u00FCell who wanted to create a stylish park for Barcelona aristocracy, the park is a designated UNESCO World Heritage Site and although many of the original plans did not come to fruition, the park remains one of the most popular visitor attractions of the city. We also visit Gaudi\u2019s home within Parc Guell. We then travel on to the church of La Sagrada Familia, Gaudi\u2019s great unfinished masterpiece. This afternoon we visit Museu Picasso for a guided tour. The collection, which includes more than 3,500 works, is strongest on Picasso\u2019s earliest years, up until 1904, which is apt considering that the artist spent his formative creative years in Barcelona.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Ch3\u003EDay 3\u003C/h3\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EWe enjoy a guided tour of the elegant Eixample Quarter of Barcelona this morning, designed during the middle of the 19th century by Ildefons Cerd\u00E0. The Quarter is full of highly original buildings in the style of art and architecture known in Catalonia as Modernisme. During our tour we visit Casa Mil\u00E0. Built between 1906 and 1910 and usually called \u2018La Pedrera\u2019, Casa Mil\u00E0 is Gaudi\u2019s greatest contribution to Barcelona\u2019s civic architecture. Casa Mil\u00E0 completely departed from the established construction principles of the time, and as a result, was ridiculed and strongly attacked by Barcelona\u2019s intellectuals. We then visit the stunning Casa Batll\u00F3 on the prestigious Passeig de Gr\u00E0cia. Designed by Gaudi for Josep Batll\u00F3, a wealthy aristocrat, this extraordinary building was designated a UNESCO World Heritage site in 2005. The rest of the day is at leisure in Barcelona, and on an individual basis you may choose to explore Las Ramblas, a vibrant district with wonderful performers, cafes and shops amid wonderful modernist architecture.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Ch3\u003EDay 4\u003C/h3\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EToday we head to Figueres, the home town of Salvador Dali. On arrival we have a guided tour of the Museo Teatro, founded in 1974 and now the most visited museum in Spain. As well as housing works by the great artist, it is also the site of his mausoleum. En route back to our hotel we visit Girona, one of Catalonia\u2019s most important cities, with its dominant cathedral and ancient medieval streets.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Ch3\u003EDay 5\u003C/h3\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EWe visit the Museu Nacional d\u2019Art de Catalunya this morning. Our guided tour on arrival introduces us to one of the most important art collections in the city, including the greatest display of Romanesque items and a Gothic collection from the whole of Spain and particularly Catalonia. We return to Barcelona Airport for our direct scheduled Easyjet flight back to Gatwick.\u003C/p\u003E\n"
          }
        },
        {
          "alias": "featurePropertyFeatureDescription",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": ""
        },
        {
          "alias": "featurePropertyFeatureSummary",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003ENB:- Please note we reserve the right to alter the above itinerary if required for operational\nreasons. Given the historic nature of the places visited, a certain degree of walking will be involved, and this holiday may not be suitable for those with mobility problems.\u003C/p\u003E\n"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
